    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0398" n="328" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg328"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Seys</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 4, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatches Nos. 9, 10, 11, and 12, of January 24th and 26th, and February 5th
                    and 6th, last. Your No. 9 has been referred to the Postmaster General.</p>
                <p>As regards the matter treated of in your No. 10, any appropriation of money for
                    the object of facilitating the emigration of freedmen to Liberia would have to
                    proceed from Congress. As that body is now adjourned, it will be impossible to
                    act on your suggestion at present. You will, however, call the attention of the
                    department to this matter again at some future session of Congress, when it
                    shall receive proper action.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Seys,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
